+# Playwright Operations, Maintenance, and Flake Policy (PW-I18)
+
+## Flake and Quarantine Policy
+- **Zero Flaky Retries**: Playwright test suites run with `retries: 0` in `playwright.config.ts`. Flaky tests are not masked by automatic retries.
+- **14-Day Quarantine Limit**: Any failing or flaky test identified in CI must be immediately quarantined using metadata tags or moved to a quarantine suite with an explicit owner and expiration date not exceeding 14 days.
+- **Permanent Skips Forbidden**: Tests cannot be permanently skipped without an active quarantine record and expiry.
+
+## Image Upgrade & Maintenance
+- **Pinned Base Image**: All test runners use the exact pinned Playwright image digest (`mcr.microsoft.com/playwright:v1.61.1-noble@sha256:...`).
+- **Upgrade Procedure**: Upgrades require updating the digest across `run.sh`, documentation, and manifest generators, followed by full execution of `make lint`, `make test`, and PR review.
+
+## Selector Hierarchy and Test Data Cleanup
+- **Selector Priority**: Prefer test IDs (`data-testid`), ARIA roles, and semantic attributes over brittle CSS/XPath selectors.
+- **Test-Data Cleanup**: Ephemeral user states, cookies, and localStorage must be isolated via separate browser contexts per test. No persistent mutated state may leak between tests.
